{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/443129-new-touchstones","id":443129,"title":"New Touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T14:50:49-07:00","id":443129,"title":"New Touchstones","content":"I'm preparing Bale Hounds werewolf pack in 2ed to confront them with PCs. I thought that good idea for this is maybe made them their personal, physical Touchstones. But when I go in to corebook examples, I hardly can relate them to NPCs in question - selfish, broken pack. I got a Bale Hound for each Deadly Sin, and for now I can only imagine that Protestant Preacher Itheaur would have as Touchstone his church - place of his religion, that is very important to him, and can be lost. But on the other hand, church is also a Locus, so by the book it should be Touchstones for his Spirit side. Any ideas maybe on broader Touchstones in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T05:02:25-07:00","id":444051,"title":"","content":"Think of the things humans can abuse as a crutch to help them get by - drugs, aspirations (someday I will be a famous writer, I don't need to waste my time with a 'real' job!), memories (the guy reliving his glory days and never growing up) - the deadly sins are a great construct for this. What is a person's weakness that helps drag them back towards cleaving to the human?<br /> <br /> There's no way to binge on Taco Bell if you can't get through the door without going into Kuruth. No way to sleep in and watch TV while riding your high if you don't have access to a soft place to nap and a working television. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T00:30:53-07:00","id":453946,"title":"","content":"Maybe I write short sum-up of Bale Hounds characters and those will help to decide what Touchstones are best for them. I only mark that that game takes place in small town of about 900 citizens on the North of Sweden. I see those Bale Bounds generally, as about Harmony 3 werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Greed</b> - Elodoth<br /> Ambitious manipulator that rules the humans in settlement by the complex net of favors to him. But as incarnation of Greed - he wants more. Put before as only middle of Hounds hierarchy, now he wants to be alpha.<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Gluttony</b> - Rahu<br /> Raindeer breeder that has taste for &quot;long pig&quot;. She has at least three human bodies in her ice room (? ch\u0142odnia ) under her house. Thinking about lowering her Harmony below 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Pride</b> - Rahu<br /> Horryfing beast that only looks sometimes as human. ( He probably is Urhanu, wolf based Uratha ). As in Blasphemies, he seed the Pride by making humans affraid of him, most often running as Urshul. Was thinking that as Flesh Touchstone he has his wolf mate, but I'm open on suggestions.<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Envy</b> - Ithaeur<br /> Protestant preacher from nighbor church that spits xenophobia and hate in his sermons. He was beta in the Hounds pack, but with leader dead, he become working Alpha. His dedicated to his work and changed his church in to massive Wound by the years of atrocities below it, wanting to start Judgment Day. By the corebook his Touchstone should be Religion, but this you cannot lose. Maybe then use church as the building for Touchstone?<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Sloth</b> - Cathalith<br /> Apathetic librarian from local library. She crushes humans dreams and reason to live by proposing defeatists books.<br /> <br /> <b>Hound of Lust</b> - Irraka<br /> Abused psychopath that thinks sex is disease and changes in to Gauru when he is with his partners. He will have lowest Harmony, maybe only 1 even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T02:24:54-07:00","id":453997,"title":"","content":"Both actually work for your Ithaeur preacher. I have the same touchstone for one of my characters. A church as a locus. I don't know that Bale Hounds even need touchstones, though. Especially since they're NPCs. Or at the most, that they all have the same spiritual touchstone, which is a Maeljin. I personally wouldn't lose any sleep over it.<br /> <br /> But if you really need to do it, think about people, places or things that your Bale Hounds would connect to or would really resonate with who they are as people. Think about people or places that your Bale Hounds would connect to. For example, your lust guy could be obsessed with an ex. You can absolutely lose Religion, by the way, though it might not fit with your plans for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}